Let $n$ be the number of people in the family, so $n=5$.
Let $x$ be the number of people who eat three eggs each day. Then $x=3$.
Let $y$ be the number of people who eat two eggs each day. Then $y = n - x = 5 - 3 = 2$.
The number of eggs eaten by the $x$ people who eat three eggs each day is $3x = 3(3) = 9$ eggs.
